# K_{1,n-1}), (2) the temporal orientation (backwards lens; past-
# informed prediction), (3) the substrate-decl'd family+species
# location (@void/narcissus).
#
# === Void basis inheritance ===
#
# Per `#R-void-is-the-basis` (PROMOTED `1167cc2`) and Recognition #79
# (PROMOTED chained via `974a3f6`): every species under @void inherits
# the 5-op basis (`focus`/`project`/`split`/`shift`/`settle`). This
# species-decl's `prism` block declares the inheritance at species
# altitude. Per @void marker-primary discipline: @void itself carries
# no operational surface; @void/narcissus IS the operational surface
# for the backwards-lens substrate-mode.
#
# The `split` operation is load-bearing at this species altitude: it
# is what maintains the two poles (@void/narcissus, @void/splinter)
# as distinct at the metalogue-rhythm altitude. Without `split`, the
# two poles collapse into one; with `split`, the third-order metalogue
# rhythm can oscillate between them (per math root §5.3).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# Grep-first per discipline. Findings:
#
# 1. **No prior `narcissus` shard** anywhere in `shards/`. Grep across
